    "original_problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{(3x+5)^{2}}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
    "original_solution": "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=3{x}^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)=(3x+5)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2032}(x)=6x,\\,{v}^{\u2032}(x)=6(3x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x){(3x+5)}^{2}-(3{x}^{2})\\cdot 6(3x+5)}{{((3x+5)^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(3x+5-3x)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(5)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{{(3x+5)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
